The next morning, we have our daily team meeting.
We are all standing together in the office.
Katrin, our team lead, begins the meeting.
"Good morning everyone," Katrin says.
"What did you do yesterday?"
Nele and Jonas talk briefly about their work.
Then Katrin looks at me.
"And Maya, how is your part of the project going?"
I am very well prepared.
"I got a lot done yesterday," I answer.
"I connected the database."
"And I programmed the new feature."
Sven, our tester, nods with satisfaction.
"Today I am writing the code for Nele's design," I continue explaining.
"Then Sven can test the software soon."
"That sounds great," Katrin says.
She notes our progress on her laptop.
She has led this team very efficiently for three years already.
I am happy that my work as a developer is going so well here.
The meeting is over after fifteen minutes, and we begin.
